## Q8: Configure and Use Azure Storage in AKS

### ✅ Step 1: Create an Azure Storage Account

az storage account create \
  --name mystorageaccount \
  --resource-group myResourceGroup \
  --location eastus \
  --sku Standard_LRS

### ✅ Step 2: Create a Storage Class (Optional)

apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: azure-disk-sc
provisioner: kubernetes.io/azure-disk
parameters:
  storageaccounttype: Standard_LRS
  kind: Managed

### ✅ Step 3: Create PVC using Azure Storage

apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: azure-pvc
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: azure-disk-sc
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 5Gi

### ✅ Step 4: Use PVC in a Pod

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-azure-storage
spec:
  containers:
    - image: nginx
      name: nginx
      volumeMounts:
        - mountPath: "/mnt/azure"
          name: azure-vol
  volumes:
    - name: azure-vol
      persistentVolumeClaim:
        claimName: azure-pvc
